### smoke-test.http
### Final step of the api-publish sequence — run this against the endpoint
### you just published (VS Code "REST Client" extension or IntelliJ HTTP
### Client syntax; both read @variables and ### request separators the same
### way).
###
### REMINDER (API-CONTRACT.md A4): for a NEW endpoint on this contract, the
### HTTP status line IS the result — check it first. Only fall back to
### reading a body-embedded result-code field if this specific module is
### still on the legacy always-200 convention (API-CONTRACT.md L1) and
### hasn't been migrated yet; know which convention applies before you read
### the response.

@baseUrl = https://{{host}}/ords/{{schemaAlias}}/{{modulePath}}
@bearerToken = {{pasteARealTokenHere}}

### 1. Auth check — cheapest possible smoke test, confirms the module, the
### base path, and Authorization: Bearer handling (A8) are all wired up
### before testing anything resource-specific.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/session
Authorization: Bearer {{bearerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Expect: 200 with the resolved identity in the body. A 401 here means the
### token is missing/invalid/expired — get a fresh one before smoke-testing
### anything else. A 403 means the token is valid but this identity has no
### access to this API/tenant.

### 2. GET collection, paginated (API-CONTRACT.md A7 — offset by default)
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{resourcesPlural}}?page_number=1&page_size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{bearerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Expect: 200, body.data (array), body.total_count, body.page_number,
### body.page_size.

### 3. GET by id (API-CONTRACT.md A2)
### Replace :id with a real id returned from request #2's data[0].id.
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{resourcesPlural}}/1
Authorization: Bearer {{bearerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Expect: 200 with the resource body, or 404 with an
### application/problem+json body if it doesn't exist (A4/A5).

### 4. POST create (API-CONTRACT.md A3 — resource-oriented, not /save)
POST {{baseUrl}}/{{resourcesPlural}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bearerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: smoke-test-{{$guid}}

{
  "name": "Smoke Test Co",
  "description": "Created by api-publish smoke test — safe to delete"
}

### Expect: 201 Created, Location header pointing at the new resource,
### response body containing its id. A 400 with an application/problem+json
### body means the request didn't parse — check the payload against
### engine-procedure-template.sql's structural-validation step. A 422 means
### it parsed fine but failed a business rule — check the problem body's
### `detail` field for which one.
###
### CLEANUP: this smoke test writes a real row. Point @baseUrl at a
### non-production schema/environment, or manually remove the "Smoke Test
### Co" row after a production smoke test — DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{resourcesPlural}}/{id}
### if a delete endpoint is published, otherwise remove it directly.

### 5. DELETE the smoke-test row (cleanup, if a delete endpoint exists —
### API-CONTRACT.md A3). Replace :id with the id returned from request #4.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{resourcesPlural}}/1
Authorization: Bearer {{bearerToken}}

### Expect: 204 No Content.
